/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/2026-10-19-arc3-r11-inspect-artifact-evidence-id-domain.md:13:Two calls on `/usr/bin/jq` returned the same outer `inspect_artifact` Evidence ID, `ev_f3b9e57f08ec6290e816552429d7e3ad1c45ef173561d6f85c9c7c0e4c06f7ca`. The same-basename copy at the alternate path returned `ev_38cc43f4175331e53c7cd1bcefea9736028dc596bf84315d75b3a86505c9613c`; the copy with a different basename returned `ev_b3ebd1711ebc131bf0acc53e27b4a4d1e404a0c494d3baa0dc0ff76c5d61f88a`. The nested `inventory_artifact` Evidence ID is `ev_bd06f056ab62f7b324a05fa29829c230998a8bf5232ed843e4dafeee60f71435` for all four calls. The generated `inspection_id` is `ai_78cf490802e595884543670257cc4f4e11b4169f1fc14e2e53c755e4168883e2` at the original path and `ai_7c39b0eafa8f1b473a78c8a51436ed1d589452cded9a7cad05e088acdc301b5b` at the same-basename alternate path.
/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/2026-10-19-arc3-r11-inspect-artifact-evidence-id-domain.md:19:The independent script in the source bundle recomputed all four reported `ev_` digests exactly. A projection check that changes only the outer subject's display name and path preserves its ID. A second check changes only `normalized_result.substeps[0].evidence.subject.local_path` and changes the outer ID; the controlled same-basename copy gives the corresponding live observation while holding the name and bytes fixed. This is consistent with the package source: `evidence.js:159-183` projects the top-level subject to digest/format/architecture but includes `normalized_result`; `artifactInspection.js:111-155` retains the nested inventory Evidence inside `normalized_result` and hashes its semantic inspection object; `canonicalDigest.js:8-25,60-76` hashes canonical JSON with SHA-256. The observed path sensitivity is specific to this `inspect_artifact` wrapper's nested result on the measured target and call shape, not a universal rule for REA Evidence IDs.
/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/2026-10-19-arc3-r11-inspect-artifact-evidence-id-domain.md:23:Only REA 6.7.0, `inspect_artifact`, this one ELF byte identity, a same-path repeat, and two alternate paths were measured. The result does not establish behavior for archive/container inputs, other verbs, other releases, other parameter values, error envelopes, or MCP-session evidence. No format-specific `open_binary` analysis, execution, network activity, or deployment claim was made. Command A's 90/90 post-integration result remains pending the co-landed corpus entry and map token.
/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/2026-10-20-r20-harmony-application-graph.md:3:recheck: inspect the retained carriers with `npx -y rea-agents@6.5.0 inspect-artifact <carrier.hap> --json`, take `normalized_result.substeps[0].evidence` verbatim as the sole `inventory_evidence` value in a JSON file, then run `npx -y rea-agents@6.5.0 project-harmony-application-graph <input.json> --json`. Exact author-side argv, cwd, UTC interval, exit, output hashes and carrier hashes are in each adjacent `receipt.json`; original bytes and input JSON are retained. The projection input Evidence has the original temporary `local_path`; a fresh run should use newly generated Evidence from the retained carrier instead of relying on that old path.
